        "metadata": {
          "category": "podcast",
          "media": {
            "duration": 5793
          },
          "description": "Australia is full of diverse Aboriginal and Torres Strait Island Nations. From the Yawuru to the Bundjalung, the clans of Zenadth Kes to the Palawa people, every mob has its own language and unique culture.  Each episode will take you on a journey to a different Nation; to listen to the sounds of Country, share some language and have a little yarn.\n\nWe’ll listen to the waves on saltwater Country and sing songs in Gumbaynggirr. We'll tell stories in the red and rocky ranges of Adnyamathanha Country. And play by the river on Yorta Yorta woka. There are hundreds of First languages to listen to and learn from!\n\nLittle Yarns is a co-listening, ABC Kids listen podcast series for pre-schoolers. Ideal for families listening together at home or as a listening resource in early learning centres, Little Yarns is all about the diverse languages, stories and Countries of Indigenous Australia.\n\nFor more music to move, podcasts to play and stories & soundtracks for sleep, download the ABC Listen app. ",
